<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">

    <!--
        A line of description text for Blizzard's settings list.

        This exists because no Blizzard element draws one. Probes G23, G25 and
        G26 settled that between them: of every template this client has, only
        the section header draws arbitrary text, and it draws it as a heading.
        SettingsLanguageRestartNeededTemplate is the only other element that
        renders text at all, and it does so as a control's label, cut off with
        an ellipsis.

        Settings.CreateElementInitializer takes any template name, not just
        Blizzard's, and G27 confirmed in game that a template an AddOn ships
        itself renders correctly in that list.

        Deliberately primitive: a plain Frame, a FontString, and an OnLoad that
        hangs one method on the frame by hand. No mixin attribute, no Blizzard
        mixin table, no inheritance. Every one of those would be a thing that
        could stop working on a client this has not been run on, for no gain.

        The FontString has a fixed width and NO height, which is what makes it
        wrap onto as many lines as it needs instead of ellipsising. That is the
        whole reason this file exists rather than reusing Blizzard's label.

        The 37px indent lines the text up with the checkbox labels below it.

        GameFontNormal, for #12. It shipped at GameFontHighlightSmall and read
        smaller than the options it describes. GameFontNormal is what the
        option labels use, and what Blizzard's own option rows use. Its yellow
        never reaches the screen, because the caller wraps the string in a
        colour escape and that is where the orange comes from, so this is a
        size change and nothing else. It is also a font object this client has
        already rendered, in the canvas panel and in the probe's own windows,
        rather than a name taken on trust.

        The 22px height is the other half of #12, reported from play: at 40 a
        one-line note left about a line and a half of dead space between it
        and the first checkbox. 22 is a little over half, which is the amount
        asked for, and it stays a FIXED height rather than becoming automatic
        because [G27] found the settings list deciding row heights on its own
        (GetExtent() returned nil and the rows still drew), so what this
        number does is not certain from here.

        What must NOT change is where the note sits: under the heading, above
        the first option it describes. Moving it below the group was suggested
        when the padding looked unfixable and is explicitly not wanted,
        because a sentence about a list belongs before the list.

        If the gap is still wrong at 22, the next thing to try is the anchor
        offset rather than another height: the FontString hangs at y=-4 from
        the frame's top.
    -->
    <Frame name="VanillaQuestingDescriptionTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size x="600" y="22"/>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <FontString parentKey="Text" inherits="GameFontNormal"
                            justifyH="LEFT" justifyV="TOP">
                    <Size x="560" y="0"/>
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOPLEFT" x="37" y="-4"/>
                    </Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad function="VanillaQuesting_DescriptionOnLoad"/>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>

</Ui>
